    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nMy neovim starts by opening the NvDash dashboard (from NvChad).\n**Most of the time** it throws the following error: \n\n```\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: ...radei/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/diff.lua:1881: Invalid buffer id: 1                           \nstack traceback:                                                              \n        [C]: in function 'nvim_buf_get_name'                                  \n        ...radei/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/diff.lua:1881: in function 'get_buf_realpath'                                                    \n        ...radei/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/diff.lua:1725: in function ''                                                                    \n        vim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\n```\n\n\nThat hasn't happened before...\nAs part of NvDash opening **a directory**, it opens an empty/unnamed buffer and deletes it right away, so `:ls` shows nothing until a file is opened.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/50fbfdf8-d6d3-4266-ab0f-02d197dd496f)\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Install mini.nvim\n2. Install nvchad/ui\n3. Enable NvDash\n4. Reopen neovim with a directory (not a file), e.g.: `nvim $HOME/.config/nvim`\n",
